{
 "name": "Decide",
 "path": "/os/system/builder/BuildGoal/Decide.goal",
 "step": [
  {
   "index": 0,
   "text": "set %threshold% = 0.5",
   "lineNumber": 18,
   "comment": "Decide which module and which action every step of this goal uses \u2014 the whole goal in two\nexchanges, not one LLM call per step.\n\nThe decider is generic: it takes a state and typed questions and answers them. It knows nothing\nabout goals or steps. Everything goal-shaped is composed HERE.\n\nThe state is built as a plang value, not rendered as JSON text: it carries step text and module\nprose, and prose contains quotes. A value serializes itself; text pasted into a JSON template\ndoes not. The questions are rendered, because they only hold module names, action names and step\nnumbers, and they point at the state by path rather than repeating it.\n\nStage 1 asks a yes/no of every (step, module) pair at once. Independent answers mean a step that\nuses three modules gets three yeses, instead of the model ranking them against each other and\ndropping two. Stage 2 then asks a closed choice \u2014 which action \u2014 only of the modules that said\nyes, and only where the module has more than one action to choose between.",
   "waitForExecution": true,
   "action": [
    {
     "module": "variable",
     "name": "set",
     "parameter": [
      {
       "name": "Name",
       "type": {
        "name": "variable"
       },
       "value": "%threshold%"
      },
      {
       "name": "Value",
       "type": {
        "name": "item"
       },
       "value": 0.5
      }
     ],
     "modifier": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "index": 1,
   "text": "set %modules% = %!app.module.list%",
   "lineNumber": 19,
   "waitForExecution": true,
   "action": [
    {
     "module": "variable",
     "name": "set",
     "parameter": [
      {
       "name": "Name",
